{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And the priests shall answer</b> in the holy tongue. <b>And they shall say: Our hands did not shed this blood.</b> And the prayer of the priests was directed to the specific Name that redeemed us from Egypt — this is what is meant by כפר לעמך ישראל אשר פדית HaShem — and do not grant permission to the attribute of strict judgment to shed innocent blood, and then ונכפר להם הדם — by the attribute of judgment and the attribute of mercy."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:49:42.331582107Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}